        "original_id": "2c14354f-a4ed-5c2d-98c3-b0c2154fc0b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean Dubuffet\n- Organizations: NME\n- Bands: Art Brut, Franz Ferdinand, The Rakes, Bloc Party, Dananananaykroyd\n- Places: South London, Glasgow, Scotland\n- Albums: You Could Have It So Much Better, Hey Everyone!\n- Concepts: outsider art, Art Wave\n\nFacts:\n- Jean Dubuffet defined outsider art as art by prisoners, loners, mentally ill people, and other marginalized people that is made without thought to imitation or presentation.\n- South London's Art Brut were named after Jean Dubuffet's definition of outsider art.\n- NME tagged South London's Art Brut as part of the Art Wave scene alongside bands including The Rakes, Franz Ferdinand, and Bloc Party.\n- Franz Ferdinand are a Scottish rock band formed in 2002 and based in Glasgow.\n- You Could Have It So Much Better is the second studio album by the Scottish indie rock band Franz Ferdinand.\n- Hey Everyone! is the debut album by the Glasgow-based rock band Dananananaykroyd, and it was released on April 6, 2009, on Best Before Records.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
